  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: "This scene demonstrates how to get and interpolate a Timeflow Channel
    by script. See the InterpolateExample object below using the script InterpTimeflowChannel.
    \n\nA Timeflow Channel may be retrieved from any TimeflowBehavior or TimeflowObject
    reference using a channel name or unique ID. Using an ID is preferred since the
    channel name may be subject to change, whereas the ID is only generated once
    when the channel is first created and does not change.\n\nOnce a channel reference
    value has been obtained, you may use one of the Interpolate methods to sample
    the channel curve at any time. See the source code for InterpTimeflowChannel.cs
    for further information"
  Warning: 'Do not serialize references to TimeflowChannel objects, otherwise it
    will result in storing a copy of the channel rather than a reference to the original. '
